<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the April 11-13 weekend, according to studio estimates collected on Sunday by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final numbers will be issued on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Anaconda .................... $16.5 million</p>
<p>    2 (1) Liar Liar ................... $14.3 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) The Saint ................... $11.2 million</p>
<p>    4 (*) Grosse Pointe Blank .........  $7.0 million</p>
<p>    5 (3) The Devil's Own .............  $4.3 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) That Old Feeling ............  $3.5 million</p>
<p>    7 (7) Jungle 2 Jungle .............  $2.3 million</p>
<p>    8 (5) Double Team .................  $2.1 million</p>
<p>    9(34) Scream ......................  $2.0 million</p>
<p>   10=(8) The 6th Man .................  $1.7 million</p>
<p>   10=(9) Return of the Jedi ..........  $1.7 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parenthesis. * = new release.</p>
<p>&quot;Anaconda,&quot; &quot;The Devil's Own&quot; and &quot;Double Team&quot; are released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; and &quot;That Old Feeling&quot; are released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;The Saint&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Grosse Pointe Blank,&quot; &quot;Jungle 2 Jungle&quot; and &quot;The 6th Man&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;Scream&quot; is released by Disney's Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Return of the Jedi&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
